        "findings": [
          {
            "id": "meaning-1",
            "category": "meaning",
            "severity": "major",
            "detail": "“It worked for four years” says the excuse had an effect for those years; “он у них был” says only that they had the excuse. Preserve the source’s point about how the excuse was used or effective.",
            "resolved": false,
            "source_anchor": {
              "quote": "They were looking for an excuse to get rid of the queer guy, and it worked for four years.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "translation_anchor": {
              "quote": "Им нужен был повод избавиться от парня-гея, и все эти четыре года он у них был.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "resolves": null
          },
          {
            "id": "register-1",
            "category": "register",
            "severity": "minor",
            "detail": "“More illegal shit” is blunt and colloquial, not “more serious illegal activity.” The translation both formalizes the voice and shifts the meaning toward seriousness; retain the source’s rough register and its emphasis on increasing illegality.",
            "resolved": false,
            "source_anchor": {
              "quote": "when Callaway started pushing the club into more illegal shit—drugs, weapons, extortion",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "translation_anchor": {
              "quote": "когда Каллауэй начал толкать клуб к более серьёзной незаконной деятельности — наркотикам, оружию, вымогательству",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "resolves": null
          },
          {
            "id": "meaning-2",
            "category": "meaning",
            "severity": "minor",
            "detail": "“Storage container” refers to a storage unit/container, whereas “камера хранения” can suggest a luggage-storage facility. Choose a rendering that preserves the storage-unit sense.",
            "resolved": false,
            "source_anchor": {
              "quote": "stored his clothes, books, and few knickknacks he’d collected over the years in a storage container.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "translation_anchor": {
              "quote": "убрал его одежду, книги и немногочисленные безделушки, которые тот собрал за эти годы, в камеру хранения.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "resolves": null
          },
          {
            "id": "style-1",
            "category": "style",
            "severity": "minor",
            "detail": "“Выразительное надбровье” is an awkward calque and does not convey “pronounced” (prominent). Recast the phrase naturally in Russian while retaining the prominent-brow image.",
            "resolved": false,
            "source_anchor": {
              "quote": "and a permanent frown lingered on his pronounced brow.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "translation_anchor": {
              "quote": "а на выразительном надбровье застыло вечное хмурое выражение.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "resolves": null
          },
          {
            "id": "meaning-3",
            "category": "meaning",
            "severity": "minor",
            "detail": "A “sneer” is contemptuous; “ухмылка” alone can be a less hostile grin. Preserve the disdain in Butch’s expression.",
            "resolved": false,
            "source_anchor": {
              "quote": "with a barely hidden sneer",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "translation_anchor": {
              "quote": "с едва скрываемой ухмылкой",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "resolves": null
          },
          {
            "id": "meaning-4",
            "category": "meaning",
            "severity": "minor",
            "detail": "“Sat sputtering after them” depicts Callaway spluttering in reaction as they left; “не мог вымолвить ни слова” instead makes him silent and unable to speak. Preserve the spluttering reaction without settling it as speechlessness.",
            "resolved": false,
            "source_anchor": {
              "quote": "while his dad sat sputtering after them.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "translation_anchor": {
